One thing that's been discussed privately, and not something we'd 
implement without a few players' approval (and some fairly widespread 
support), is a Grand Master status for the trophies which have a 
definite _best_ that would give that player a permanent victory but 
render them no longer eligible for that trophy.

To date that would cover:

	Best of 13                 -   marvin (twice)
	Highest Scored Ascension   -   eit_brad

It would later cover Best Behaved Ascension, if anyone manages a perfect 
12 on it.  I suppose it could cover Lowest Scored Ascension at _some_ 
point, if we ever come up with a theoretical minimum and someone manages 
to achieve it ... ;-)

A possible, though not necessarily desirable, extension to this would be 
to choose a moderately arbitrary "best" value for the other Major 
trophies so that they could be included in this as well.

This shouldn't be taken as an attempt to "stop" marvin; I'm just 
bringing it up since we want some public discussion before we do this 
and this thread is already discussing a similar topic.  There are two 
major benefits in this, one for the players who'd be Grand Mastered and 
one for the Tournament:

1)	not having any expectation that he repeat the Best of 13 every year 
would free him up to try some new and challenging things, like trying 
for the perfect 12 on Best Behaved Ascension

2)	this would make the top rankings of the Tournament more competitive, 
which would increase the tension and interest in those trophies.  We 
hear from lots of folks every year who say they won't be playing, since 
"marvin always wins".

On the other hand, we're also quite happy to watch in awe as marvin goes 
on year after year, if only out of curiosity to see how long he can keep 
going.  ;-)

What do y'all think?

